    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d218">

                <pb facs="0637" n="423" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg423"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 200.</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Moran to Mr. Fish</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 193.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1871-01-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 19, 1871</date>. (Received February
                    3.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Referring to my No. 164, I have now the
                    honor to send herewith copies, extracted from the Times of the 11th, 13th, and
                    18th instant, of the reports of the proceedings against the ship International
                    for violating <pb facs="0638" n="424" xml:id="pg424"/> the neutrality or foreign
                    enlistment act of 1870, together with an editorial from the Times of the 18th on
                    the subject.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>BENJAMIN MORAN.</signed></closer>





